        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\n\nFor the first query, [a,b,c,d]=[A1,B1,C1,D1]=[2,3,4,1][a, b, c, d] = [A_1, B_1, C_1, D_1] = [2, 3, 4, 1][a,b,c,d]=[A1​,B1​,C1​,D1​]=[2,3,4,1]. It is optimal to buy 222 doses of Covaxin (2+5=7)(2+5=7)(2+5=7) and 222 doses of Covishield (4+5=9)(4+5=9)(4+5=9). So the total money spent is 7+9=167+9=167+9=16 and now the black marketeer cannot buy any more doses. So the answer is 4.\n\n\nFor the second query, [a,b,c,d]=[A2,B2,C2,D2]=[(2+11⋅4) mod 20+3,(3+11⋅4) mod 20+7,(4+11⋅4) mod 20+8,(1+11⋅4) mod 20+4]=[9,14,16,9][a, b, c, d] = [A_2, B_2, C_2, D_2] = [(2 + 11\\cdot 4)\\bmod 20 + 3, (3 + 11\\cdot 4) \\bmod 20 + 7, (4 + 11\\cdot 4) \\bmod 20 + 8, (1 + 11\\cdot 4) \\bmod 20 + 4]=[9, 14, 16, 9][a,b,c,d]=[A2​,B2​,C2​,D2​]=[(2+11⋅4)mod20+3,(3+11⋅4)mod20+7,(4+11⋅4)mod20+8,(1+11⋅4)mod20+4]=[9,14,16,9].\n\n\nFor the third and the last query, [a,b,c,d]=[A3,B3,C3,D3]=[3,12,15,4][a, b, c, d] = [A_3, B_3, C_3, D_3] = [3, 12, 15, 4][a,b,c,d]=[A3​,B3​,C3​,D3​]=[3,12,15,4]."
      }
